# The film's timing — the beat table's one machine-read home.
#
# One BEATDRIFT row per seed, verbatim as `probes/CensusBeatDrift` printed it, at the tree
# the row's own `sha=` names. `probes/bench.sh` hands this file to the probe with
# --baseline-file, so the judged row compares today's ticks against these and the sweep goes
# red when a beat slides further than the declared band.
#
# Blank lines and lines opening with `#` are ignored. Every other line must open with
# `BEATDRIFT ` and must carry the `ticks=` the sweep runs at: a row measured at another
# budget is refused rather than compared, because two budgets are two questions and the
# difference would report itself as drift.
#
# Moving the pin is these rows re-measured, in the commit that moves the film, with the sha
# they were measured at riding in the rows themselves. `git log -p -- probes/beatdrift.baseline`
# is then the whole move history, kept by git, which cannot drift from the value it explains —
# the discipline .github/canonical-digest already keeps for the seal. docs/ARCHITECTURE.md's
# census entry 2 keeps the narrative table of recorded commits and the per-step verdicts; this
# file is the row the bench actually reads.
#
# Re-measure from a pinned tree (D-030 clause 3 — an exported tree has no .git to ask, which
# is what --sha is for):
#
#     git archive <sha> | tar -x -C "$WORK" && cd "$WORK"
#     javac -encoding UTF-8 --release 17 -d out $(find src -name '*.java')
#     javac -encoding UTF-8 --release 17 -cp out -d probes/out probes/*.java
#     java -cp out:probes/out CensusBeatDrift 42,7 6000 --sha <short>

BEATDRIFT sha=a7660c2 seed=42 ticks=6000 birth=1299 refusal=1525 overflow=4289 flatline=4289 peace=4309 reboot=4329 door=4329 second_birth=5229 max_delta=n/a
BEATDRIFT sha=a7660c2 seed=7 ticks=6000 birth=1259 refusal=1525 overflow=3707 flatline=3707 peace=3727 reboot=3747 door=3747 second_birth=4659 max_delta=n/a
